# Licensing, Source-Available Non-Commercial Scope, and Legal Notices

This repository is an experimental **Research Proof-of-Concept (PoC)** for
cross-ISA system virtualization and graphics protocol interoperability. It is
**not** an end-user product, turnkey installer, or production virtual machine
monitor.

Because this workspace combines patches to existing free/open-source upstreams
with independent research harnesses, bare-metal test firmware, and technical
documentation, different directories are governed by distinct license terms as
specified below. Full canonical license texts are provided in `LICENSES/`.

---

## 1. Upstream Patches (`patches/`) — Governed by Upstream Licenses

Modifications to third-party open-source projects under `patches/` are
distributed strictly under each upstream project's original license, with **no
additional restrictions** beyond those licenses:

- **`patches/qemu-platform/`** (for QEMU):
  GNU General Public License, version 2 only (**`GPL-2.0-only`**) — see
  `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt`. Original upstream copyright notices and patch
  authorship headers are preserved.
- **`patches/reims/`** and **`patches/metal2vulkan/`** (for `reims-vgpu` and
  `metal2vulkan`):
  Dual-licensed under GNU General Public License version 2 or later
  (**`GPL-2.0-or-later`**) OR GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 or
  later (**`LGPL-3.0-or-later`**), at your option — see
  `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt`, `LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt`, and
  `LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-or-later.txt`. (When linked into the `GPL-2.0-only` QEMU
  executable, the `GPL-2.0` option applies.)
- **External reference patch (`patches/upstream-reference/`):**
  Anees Iqbal's reference `vmapple-usb-chardev.patch` from
  `steelbrain/experiment-macOS-arm64-on-asahi-linux-arm64` (commit `657bb24`) is
  not relicensed by this project; public snapshots do not redistribute its patch
  text and instead fetch it directly from its pinned upstream commit via
  `./tools/fetch-sources.sh`.

---

## 2. Original PoC Code, Bare-Metal Probes, Tools & Documentation — Source-Available, Noncommercial Only

All original files authored by this project outside `patches/` — including
self-authored probes, harnesses, test suites, build scripts, `Makefile`,
`sources.lock.json`, `docs/`, and `README*` — are **source-available**
under the **PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0**
(`LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.txt`,
<https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0>). Note that
PolyForm Noncommercial is a source-available non-commercial license, not an
OSI-approved open-source license.

Pursuant to the *Notices* section of the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0,
every copy or redistribution of any part of these original materials must
retain the following required notices verbatim:

Required Notice: Copyright (c) 2026 macos-local research contributors. Licensed under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (<https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0>). Commercial use, commercial distribution, sale, paid installation/configuration service, commercial bundling, or commercial cloud/compute hosting of these PolyForm-licensed materials is not permitted under this license.

Required Notice: Non-Endorsement and Anti-Commercialization — Neither the name of this repository nor the identifiers of its contributors may be used to endorse, promote, advertise, or imply affiliation with any derivative software, prebuilt image, hardware bundle, or third-party service without prior written permission. The contributors have authorized NO commercial party to sell, host, or support these PolyForm-licensed proof-of-concept materials.

Required Notice: Experimental Research PoC Disclaimer — Provided strictly "AS IS" without warranty of any kind. This software does NOT provide a security boundary or isolation sandbox, and abnormal termination may corrupt virtual disk state. All execution risks rest solely with the user.

### Upstream Free-Software Contribution Carve-Out

To avoid impeding upstream open-source collaboration where upstream policies
permit, maintainers of the open-source projects patched in Section 1 (`QEMU`,
`reims-vgpu`, `metal2vulkan`) are additionally granted
permission to incorporate self-authored, Apple-code-free platform tests or build
helpers from this repository into their respective official open-source
repositories under those projects' existing open-source licenses. This carve-out
grants **no** rights for closed-source or standalone commercial redistribution.

